=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4403f15-4d99-556e-baff-d5374b2c5b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4403f15-4d99-556e-baff-d5374b2c5b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303293} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c91ff50-1701-5eb5-9b4f-99237b8d8226" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7cbbaf2-6a2c-5981-8af6-1993d3e9c447" :question/math-academy-id "q-316585" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/7edace8cab645caab8309768ede92f534281567640aba7082f647ca1c8a49074.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,3\\,|\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c466f5-12a2-5326-8360-dbac1c75312e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284006} {:answer/id #uuid "b9767f93-7e87-508f-bcf9-fd3a7cebce9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c466f5-12a2-5326-8360-dbac1c75312e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284006} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2dd50da-f51e-570d-a033-74dc33383755" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bca98248-d03b-5f6b-b96d-7295f22821a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316591" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/455e0a08e2a0929a60d7fa1b76973e1b7a460efe8cc1cf01719ce211feacd8c0.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-5\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a36cd622-9700-5d2a-98fd-764e0be6bc9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303297} {:answer/id #uuid "04113139-bdaf-5a64-9ae1-649d8e783b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a36cd622-9700-5d2a-98fd-764e0be6bc9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303297} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a6df28c-19d0-5a33-9a46-56de57b84f98" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdb91b39-1c5d-5d35-ae0e-6b0f9f93b532" :question/math-academy-id "q-316601" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -9 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=0\\cdot 1-(-9)\\cdot 4=36.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,36\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e7464d-7629-5806-aa07-04e5640e39cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284009} {:answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "067bb28f-70ae-5ca2-916c-78f24134099e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284010} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c99caa6-f201-5a73-979b-5074f5344bf3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d412caa5-3690-592c-8eec-aa466eedc1b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-316606" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1),(5,1),(3,4).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/3e2c56766f201095bee0eea101b877e30910c676c998f37d261fd7cf7aabb837.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-6\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758a80e2-fef0-5d0c-9131-acf560683f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284013} {:answer/id #uuid "042bfcba-1272-5a6d-b6f0-b3e1d9655a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "758a80e2-fef0-5d0c-9131-acf560683f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284013} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a06e39e-da10-5b2b-801f-8c68b17f7337" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "423d63ac-43bc-545e-9007-0b2aae970538" :question/math-academy-id "q-316607" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(0,0),(6,0),(2,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/059560835586e9c149cdb5dabcddc80610a58bfa0c30cb5f685b8bb6bdca3e90.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 5=15.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "706f557a-719f-52f6-9e63-2d3f4b2d9d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284033} {:answer/id #uuid "5b50e6e2-80aa-5a06-9b77-0391e59a6f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284034} {:answer/id #uuid "55e29dc6-9969-527f-814b-5543bd045230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284035} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef67f89-9929-56ca-b481-9b7c306ac8c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/va